 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Bong-Soo Sohn and Chandrajit Bajaj [S1]. It is based on concepts from Morse theory, using the contour tree to capture changes in the topology of a scalar field at critical points [S1]. The approach addresses the challenge of finding correspondence between contours of consecutive isosurfaces in time-varying data, such as hemoglobin dynamics and turbulent vortex simulations [S1]. The Topology Change Graph (TCG) was developed to visualize these topological events and aid in interactive feature selection [S1].
